# The ENUM cell of `t1019`'s check-time method-existence rule — and the cell
# that shows why the rule had to land WITH the `t1017` dispatch fix rather than
# after it.
#
# `Color.Red().is_ok()` used to be accepted and to print `false`: the dispatch
# gate intercepted the four names `is_some` / `is_none` / `is_ok` / `is_error`
# for every receiver and folded a non-Option/Result one to a constant. `false`
# is even the RIGHT-LOOKING answer for a plain enum, which is exactly why the
# whole class hid for so long. Now the four names fall through to the ordinary
# dispatch, and an enum that has no such method is REJECTED here instead of
# reaching the linker.
#
# The POSITIVE CONTROL is `match`, the way you actually ask an enum which
# variant it is: it must keep working in the same program.
enum Color:
    Red()
    Green()

int rank(Color c):
    match c:
        case Color.Red():
            return 1
        else:
            return 2

void main():
    Color c = Color.Red()
    print(rank(c))
    print(c.is_ok())
